# The field holds a whole number in 64 bits. counter.count++ is a 64-bit addition and one test that the sum is still a whole number the field can hold. That test stays: nothing bounds the field.
# WIDE-LABEL: name="bump" role=Source
# WIDE: Int64 b@[[count]] = Load(b@[[counter]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# WIDE: Int64 b@[[next]] = Add(b@[[count]], $1(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:Increment)
# WIDE: Int32 b@[[fits]] = LessEqual(b@[[next]], $4503599627370495(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:TypeTest)
# WIDE-NEXT: Branch(b@[[fits]], Terminal, {{*}}:TypeTest)
# WIDE-NEXT: Successors: Then:#{{*}}, Else:Rare:#{{*}}
# WIDE: Store(b@[[next]], b@[[counter]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields{{*}}:PutSlot)
# WIDE-LABEL: end of function
# x86-64 adds one to the low half of the field in memory. Only a carry out of that half takes the rare arm, which takes the one back, adds in 64 bits and tests the bound.
# HALF-LABEL: name="bump" role=Source
# HALF: Int32 b@[[low]] = Load(b@[[counter]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:PutSlot)
# HALF: Int32 b@[[next]] = Add(b@[[low]], $1(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:PutSlot)
# HALF-NEXT: Store(b@[[next]], b@[[counter]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields{{*}}:PutSlot)
# HALF-NEXT: Int32 b@[[hasCarried]] = Below(b@[[next]], $1(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:PutSlot)
# HALF-NEXT: Branch(b@[[hasCarried]], Terminal, {{*}}:PutSlot)
# HALF-NEXT: Successors: Then:Rare:#{{*}}, Else:#{{*}}
# HALF-LABEL: end of function
# The addition, the store and the branch on the carry are one instruction of x86-64.
